Subject: Precompute the AOT inline-hit offsets and add the compiled slow paths

What this does
  Gives the generated unit the constants and the engine entry points it needs
  to inline the hot property and arithmetic fast paths, and adds the engine
  side of the slow paths those inlines fall back to.

Why we need it
  The unit is a separate translation unit, so every call to an
  `always_inline` engine helper is a real call across the boundary. Measured
  on box2d, the compiled named read alone was 32.1M calls, the numeric boxing
  pair 30.4M and the tagged-arithmetic helper 10.9M. Inlining them needs the
  struct offsets and enum values the generated code compares against, and a
  miss must continue compiled rather than leave for the interpreter, or a cold
  or polymorphic site disables its function.

What it adds
  js_aot_gen_layout()      - the JSRegPIC size and field offsets, the entry
                             kind and no-site markers, the lazy-JSON tag, the
                             binary and unary sub-operation values used by the
                             inline paths, and the byte and mask of
                             JSObject.is_prototype (found by setting the
                             bit-field in a zeroed object); all covered by the
                             layout hash
  qjs_aot_pic_holder()     - the frame's PIC holder-shape array, loaded once
                             at entry
  qjs_aot_read_field_slow() - the cache-filling read; drops a quickened `_own`
                             opcode back to its generic one when the fill
                             leaves the site without an own slot
  qjs_aot_put_field_slow()  - the cached add transition then the cache-filling
                             write; publishes `ip` for a setter's backtrace
  qjs_aot_cmp_take()        - the generic compare branch (regvm_cmp_take)
  qjs_aot_get_global_hit()  - the site-cache hit alone, running no user code
  qjs_aot_branch_cmp()      - handles the fused strict compare against
                             undefined as a tag test on `a`
  qjs_aot_own_read_hit()    - refuses a site when the frame has no PIC yet
  qjs_aot_fitsi()           - static inline in quickjs-aot-rt.h
  qjs_aot_box_num()         - static inline in quickjs-aot-rt.h

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

Notes
  The inline helpers live in the generated unit and use only the offsets above,
  so the engine keeps its own out-of-line copies. Boxing stays bit-identical
  (-0 remains a float); `types.js`, `--check-locals` and the wrong-profile test
  all pass, and box2d's checksum is unchanged.

